      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on the wiki, here\u0027s how the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment:\n\nThe Hub **never holds the key in its own process environment at all.** Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. **The key is injected only into child-process environments** \u2014 specifically, it\u0027s injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent (and Query agent) child processes immediately before they start.\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 the key is never written to or stored in the Hub\u0027s own environment variables.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaving, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, because the key simply doesn\u0027t exist there. The credential exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API.\n\nSee [[credential-scoping]] for more details.",
